drm/msm/a6xx: take the A650 UBWC highest bank bit from the UBWC config

Holodor (2026-10-01), companion to 0700. In 7.1.2 a6xx_calc_ubwc_config() forces
highest_bank_bit = 16 for A650 ("TODO: get ddr type from bootloader and use 15 for
LPDDR4") and only warns when the shared UBWC config disagrees, while the display (DPU)
uses the shared config: with 0700 on an LPDDR4X SM8250 that left GPU=16 vs DPU=15
("Inconclusive highest_bank_bit value: 16 (GPU) vs 15 (UBWC_CFG)", RP5 boot log).
For A650 take the shared value (SMEM-derived since 0007/0008/0700). Mainline (7.3) has
since dropped this per-GPU override entirely and uses the shared config as-is.
Other GPUs are untouched.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gpu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gpu.c
@@ -776,8 +776,14 @@
 	if (adreno_is_a623(gpu))
 		cfg->highest_bank_bit = 16;
 
-	if (adreno_is_a650(gpu) ||
-	    adreno_is_a660(gpu) ||
+	/*
+	 * A650 (SM8250) shipped with both LPDDR4X (HBB 15) and LPDDR5 (HBB 16);
+	 * the UBWC config now derives it from SMEM, so take it from there.
+	 */
+	if (adreno_is_a650(gpu))
+		cfg->highest_bank_bit = common_cfg->highest_bank_bit;
+
+	if (adreno_is_a660(gpu) ||
 	    adreno_is_a690(gpu) ||
 	    adreno_is_a730(gpu) ||
 	    adreno_is_a740_family(gpu)) {
